# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 2: fair_price), edited.

~ baltus_start
Narrator: The Trading Post smells of tallow and damp wool, with a polished brass scale gleaming on the counter.
baltus_tolliver [weary]: A merchant lives by honest measure, friends, yet Eleanor Heyling sells fine rag paper across the Round for less than the mill charges. Glance at her ledger for me, and learn how she keeps her purse full.
* We will look -> baltus_accept
* Not our business -> END

~ baltus_accept
baltus_tolliver [smile]: Boundlessly grateful. A quiet look at her columns is all a fair man asks.
quest a_fair_price asked
set price_asked
-> END

~ eleanor_visit
Narrator: Dry parchment and walnut gall scent the narrow shelves, and an open account book rests beside Eleanor's elbow.
eleanor_heyling [neutral]: If Baltus sent you to whine about vellum, tell him to scrape the lead out from under his brass scale first. Have you come to read, or just to hover?
* [Investigation DC 12] Study her ledger over her shoulder -> ledger_ok | ledger_fail
* Ask her side of it -> eleanor_side
* Leave -> END

~ eleanor_side
eleanor_heyling [angry]: Every pound of lampblack ink from his counter weighs fourteen ounces by any honest iron. I price my sheets so the schoolhouse does not have to beg him for scraps.
-> eleanor_visit

~ ledger_ok
Narrator: {name} traces the neat red ink along the margin: the loss on every quire is covered by a quiet newcomer fund signed by Finneas Trout.
eleanor_heyling [sly]: Sharp eyes. Finneas and I see to it our people have paper without paying a tithe to the Old Ways.
set price_ledger_seen
-> END

~ ledger_fail
Narrator: Her hand drops flat over the page before {name} can make sense of the cramped figures.
eleanor_heyling [neutral]: This book is not for sale, stranger. If you want sums, bother Tamsin Ledger up at the Mayor's House.
-> END

~ tamsin_audit
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Two merchants accusing each other of arithmetic is the dullest sin in Wickermoor. For ten gold to cover my candles, I will audit both books before the sixth bell.
* Pay ten gold -> audit_paid
* Another way -> END

~ audit_paid
gold -10
Narrator: By next candle-mark, Tamsin lays a single sheet of foolscap on the desk, smelling faintly of cold tea.
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Baltus thumbs his brass pan by two drams, and Eleanor covers her cheap paper with a schoolhouse grant from Finneas Trout. Both books balance, if you squint.
set price_ledger_seen
-> END

~ broker
baltus_tolliver [sly]: You have the look of folks who have seen the bottom of the inkwell. Come, how do we settle our dear neighbour?
* Broker a truce -> truce
* Tell Baltus where her money comes from -> side_baltus
* Tell Eleanor his scale is rigged -> side_eleanor

~ truce
baltus_tolliver [neutral]: Let her hear your proposal, then, though I doubt city ears take kindly to country sense.
* [Persuasion DC 13] Argue a fair price for both -> truce_ok | truce_fail

~ truce_ok
baltus_tolliver [smile]: Paper to her shelves, ink to mine, and no more bleeding the penny tray. I can live with that.
eleanor_heyling [neutral]: So long as your weights stay honest, Mr. Tolliver, we have an accord.
set price_outcome = "truce"
quest a_fair_price done
gold +30
standing cult +1
standing newcomers +1
-> END

~ truce_fail
eleanor_heyling [angry]: I will not take lectures on fairness from a man with a heavy thumb.
baltus_tolliver [weary]: You see how she is, friends.
-> broker

~ side_baltus
baltus_tolliver [sly]: A schoolhouse grant from poor Finneas? Wait until the Round hears the newcomers need charity just to write a letter.
set price_outcome = "baltus"
quest a_fair_price done
gold +25
standing cult +1
standing newcomers -1
-> END

~ side_eleanor
eleanor_heyling [smile]: Two drams of lead under the pan, tested in front of the whole Round. Look how red his ears are.
set price_outcome = "eleanor"
quest a_fair_price done
gold +25
standing cult -1
standing newcomers +1
-> END
